        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. King Charles' visit to US goes ahead despite Washington shooting Issued on: 27/04/2026 - 11:08 King Charles' state visit to the U.S. will go ahead as planned on ​Monday despite a shooting at a White House dinner attended by President Donald Trump, Buckingham Palace said after discussions with U.S. officials. The four-day trip - which is to include a private meeting with Trump and an address to Congress marking 250 years since U.S. independence — is intended to reinforce the strained U.S.-British relationship ‌amid differences over the Iran war. Investigators probe motives of US press gala shooting suspect 27/04/2026 Trump calls suspect in press dinner attack 'pretty sick guy' 27/04/2026 'Unable to cope': Malian army, Wagner 'overstretched' by Tuareg separatists and jihadist militants 27/04/2026 Africa King Charles state visit to US to go on as planned after shooting 26/04/2026 Europe Russian mercenaries in Mali: Limited gains, reports of abuse 26/04/2026 Africa Trump turns assassination attempts into 'political rocket fuel' 26/04/2026 Americas Malian Defence Minister Sadio Camara killed by rebels 26/04/2026 Africa Gunfire and blasts rock Mali: Army claims situation is under control 26/04/2026 Africa Chernobyl 40th anniversary: A zone that must be sheltered 26/04/2026 Europe"
