        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump calls suspect in press dinner attack 'pretty sick guy' Issued on: 27/04/2026 - 11:01 U.S. President Donald Trump said on Sunday that the suspect accused of trying to attack administration officials at a ​black-tie gala on Saturday night was a \"pretty sick guy\" who had been flagged to law enforcement by family members. Trump said in TV interviews that the suspect, whom an official identified as 31-year-old Cole Tomas Allen, of Torrance, California, had posted what Trump described as an \"anti-Christian\" manifesto. 'Unable to cope': Malian army, Wagner 'overstretched' by Tuareg separatists and jihadist militants 27/04/2026 Africa King Charles state visit to US to go on as planned after shooting 26/04/2026 Europe Russian mercenaries in Mali: Limited gains, reports of abuse 26/04/2026 Africa Trump turns assassination attempts into 'political rocket fuel' 26/04/2026 Americas Malian Defence Minister Sadio Camara killed by rebels 26/04/2026 Africa Gunfire and blasts rock Mali: Army claims situation is under control 26/04/2026 Africa Chernobyl 40th anniversary: A zone that must be sheltered 26/04/2026 Europe 40 years since Chernobyl disaster: Soviet Union's 'top-down culture' partly to blame 26/04/2026 Europe Deadly Israeli strikes hit Lebanon despite ceasefire extension 26/04/2026 Middle East"
